## Business Recommendations
Amazon sellers should move away from broad, discount-heavy strategies and focus instead on smarter pricing, clearer product segmentation, and stronger brand positioning. Reclassifying the oversized “Other” category should be a priority, as better product categorisation would improve pricing precision, promotional targeting, and customer clarity. High-performing cable types like HDMI and Lightning should be positioned more strategically as premium offerings, while highly rated brands should receive stronger visibility through sponsored placements and merchandising. Rather than assuming deeper discounts drive engagement, sellers should use testing and data to identify more profitable discount ranges that maintain customer trust without sacrificing margin. Overall, the biggest opportunity lies in shifting from generic promotional tactics toward more structured, brand- and category-led growth strategies.


